            <ArticleTitle>[Measures combating pre-hospital sudden death].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>809-12</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To study pre-hospital sudden death so as to reduce the death rate.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">814 pre-hospital deaths were randomly selected from January 1990 to May 1994 for a retrospective study.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">616 deaths (75.7%) showed a history of cardiac disease and hypertension. The age for high sudden death rate ranged from 50 to 69 years (53.9%). Most of the cases (87.8%) were found in their homes. 21 cases (2.58%) successfully recovered.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The key points to improve the success rate of pre-hospital sudden death are: completing Beijing Emergency Medical Center's emergency care network so as to decrease the emergency care radium and shorten the emergency care time; disseminating emergency care knowledge on CPR and CPR technique.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
